WEBVTT

00:09.009 --> 00:11.428
EMERGENCY MEDICAL CENTER

00:18.935 --> 00:20.311
Give me a sedative.

00:20.395 --> 00:21.312
What do we do?

00:21.396 --> 00:23.815
- Calm down and wait here.
- My mom is very sick.

00:23.898 --> 00:24.983
Then how long…

00:25.692 --> 00:27.986
She couldn't sleep yesterday.

00:28.069 --> 00:30.572
We'll get to them soon, so wait a bit.

00:31.740 --> 00:34.242
Coming through.

00:36.453 --> 00:37.746
KANGBUK SAMSUNG HOSPITAL

00:37.829 --> 00:40.081
Doctor, please…

00:40.165 --> 00:43.001
Out of the way, please!

00:43.084 --> 00:46.546
You need to stay with me. Open your eyes!

01:10.236 --> 01:11.821
- Thank you.
- Sure.

01:18.870 --> 01:19.704
Mom.

01:20.830 --> 01:21.664
Yes?

01:36.304 --> 01:37.555
I'm sorry.

01:45.772 --> 01:46.606
Let's go.

02:27.063 --> 02:30.733
BLOODHOUNDS

02:30.817 --> 02:32.068
KANGBUK SAMSUNG HOSPITAL

02:32.152 --> 02:34.112
- Mr. An Mun-ju?
- Yes.

02:40.160 --> 02:42.579
You're very lucky
there wasn't any nerve damage.

02:43.872 --> 02:45.415
Will you undergo scar removal?

02:45.915 --> 02:48.626
We've sealed up the wound,

02:48.710 --> 02:52.422
but you should get the procedure quickly
if you don't want it to leave a scar.

02:52.505 --> 02:53.590
It's expensive, right?

02:53.673 --> 02:55.425
I can give you a referral.

02:56.384 --> 02:59.637
Here. Look at this photo
of a recent procedure.

03:00.180 --> 03:02.849
- Do you see the scar on his forehead?
- Yes.

03:02.932 --> 03:05.226
This is the photo before the procedure.

03:05.310 --> 03:07.437
This is after the laser procedure.

03:07.520 --> 03:08.396
I see.

03:08.479 --> 03:10.773
It's your face, and you're still young.

03:10.857 --> 03:13.568
I think it would be best
to have the procedure.

03:15.570 --> 03:17.655
No, it's fine. Thank you.

03:19.532 --> 03:21.576
Is there a Choi Han-seon?

03:22.493 --> 03:23.703
Yes, please come in.

03:23.786 --> 03:24.621
Woo-jin.

03:28.833 --> 03:29.667
Are you all right?

03:31.294 --> 03:32.921
- Let me see.
- No.

03:33.588 --> 03:34.589
Let me see.

03:42.096 --> 03:43.348
Jeez.

03:46.976 --> 03:48.269
How many stitches you get?

03:49.187 --> 03:50.146
Thirty stitches.

03:50.230 --> 03:54.025
Jeez. Those motherfuckers.
This is seriously pissing me off.

03:56.194 --> 03:57.028
Let's report it.

03:59.489 --> 04:02.242
If you call the cops, your mom dies.

04:08.164 --> 04:10.083
- I can't.
- Why not?

04:10.166 --> 04:11.834
That might put my mom in danger.

04:13.795 --> 04:15.171
Fuck, seriously.

04:15.964 --> 04:17.548
Right. What about the contract?

04:19.300 --> 04:21.511
Right. Look.

04:22.220 --> 04:25.098
I've never heard of
a "loan extension fee."

04:25.181 --> 04:26.474
You have to pay 10%

04:26.557 --> 04:29.477
of the principal every week
until you pay off the loan.

04:29.560 --> 04:32.981
Your mom took out a loan of 50 million,
so the fee alone is five million.

04:33.064 --> 04:35.358
But once you miss a payment, it doubles.

04:35.441 --> 04:37.819
The interest rate rises from 5% to 20%.

04:37.902 --> 04:41.155
These bastards wrote it in the fine print
so people wouldn't catch it.

04:41.239 --> 04:43.574
This is a scam. Your mom stood no chance.

04:44.075 --> 04:45.076
What should I do?

04:45.159 --> 04:47.078
Pay it back immediately.

04:47.161 --> 04:50.039
Your interest will go up to 100 million.
Your house is collateral.

04:50.790 --> 04:52.166
We don't have the money.

04:53.543 --> 04:56.296
Damn it. Fuck, seriously.

05:03.261 --> 05:04.178
Let's eat first.

05:04.262 --> 05:06.180
What do you want to eat? I'm buying.

05:09.434 --> 05:10.393
Rib eye.

05:11.477 --> 05:13.688
You really have the energy
to joke around right now?

05:14.355 --> 05:15.773
I really want rib eye.

05:16.983 --> 05:17.859
Okay.

05:19.152 --> 05:21.738
I'll buy you stir-fried pork.
It's as good as rib eye.

05:23.865 --> 05:24.741
It's okay.

05:25.450 --> 05:27.076
STIR-FRIED PORK
KIMCHI STEW

05:27.160 --> 05:29.329
I always come here after a workout.

05:29.412 --> 05:31.331
It's a routine. A perfect one.

05:31.414 --> 05:34.459
Don't say a word and eat, understood?

05:34.542 --> 05:37.086
- Understood.
- Hey!

05:37.170 --> 05:39.213
It's so good to see you.

05:39.297 --> 05:41.049
- Oh my.
- Two orders of stir-fried pork.

05:41.132 --> 05:42.967
Okay, who is your new friend?

05:43.051 --> 05:44.844
- Hello.
- He's my boxing friend.

05:44.927 --> 05:46.179
Is that right?

05:51.893 --> 05:53.811
- I need to take this call.
- Okay.

05:54.645 --> 05:58.691
Hello, this is Woo-jin. How've you been?

05:59.901 --> 06:01.486
Well, the thing is…

06:08.368 --> 06:09.952
MY SON

06:11.454 --> 06:12.497
Hey, Gun-woo.

06:13.081 --> 06:14.832
Woo-jin looked at the contract.

06:14.916 --> 06:16.709
Those people are professional con men.

06:16.793 --> 06:20.046
There's no way it could've been avoided.
It's not your fault, Mom.

06:20.129 --> 06:21.714
Thank you, my son.

06:23.299 --> 06:25.968
What did they say about your face?

06:26.719 --> 06:28.429
They say it's healing nicely.

06:28.930 --> 06:30.348
That's a relief.

06:31.391 --> 06:33.518
I'll clean up the café later with Woo-jin.

06:33.601 --> 06:35.520
You should rest at home today.

06:37.021 --> 06:40.608
No, I will clean it up.
Just leave it alone, okay?

06:40.691 --> 06:43.653
It's fine. I will do it
on my way back home, okay?

06:43.736 --> 06:45.238
Your food is ready.

06:48.658 --> 06:51.828
Mom, I'll call you back on my way home.

06:51.911 --> 06:53.663
- All right.
- Okay.

07:00.086 --> 07:02.964
Help me out just this once.

07:03.047 --> 07:05.341
It's not for me, but for a friend of mine.

07:05.842 --> 07:08.928
I'll pay the principal and interest
on time. There'll be no issues.

07:10.054 --> 07:13.391
We can get a 2% interest loan
from other places too. Please, come on.

07:13.891 --> 07:15.726
Please give me a 1% loan.

07:15.810 --> 07:17.937
I'm begging you. Just this once.

07:18.521 --> 07:20.690
It's because I really care about this kid.

07:22.024 --> 07:23.192
Please help me out.

07:23.276 --> 07:25.653
Do you know how many loan payments
I collected for you?

07:26.320 --> 07:28.197
I did that for you
with no strings attached.

07:58.019 --> 07:59.979
Why didn't you call me?

08:00.062 --> 08:01.647
It just came out.

08:02.523 --> 08:03.524
Have some.

08:03.608 --> 08:06.068
This is the tastiest
spicy stir-fried pork in Korea.

08:12.950 --> 08:14.035
- Right?
- Yes.

08:14.118 --> 08:14.952
Let's eat.

08:26.172 --> 08:28.925
LET'S TALK AT THE OFFICE

08:29.008 --> 08:32.303
He has a short temper,
so just keep your head down for a bit.

08:32.803 --> 08:34.138
Let me do the talking.

08:34.222 --> 08:35.056
Okay.

08:37.767 --> 08:39.560
- Mr. Seo.
- Yes?

08:39.644 --> 08:41.020
How much is this?

08:41.687 --> 08:43.397
That should be around 20 million won.

08:43.481 --> 08:45.942
Brother! Woo-jin is here!

08:47.401 --> 08:49.904
Hey, you bastard. You have some nerve,

08:49.987 --> 08:52.114
popping up all of a sudden,
asking for money.

08:52.198 --> 08:54.575
You think I have anything nice to say?

08:55.076 --> 08:56.911
- Jeez, I'm sorry.
- Forget it.

08:56.994 --> 08:58.037
Come on.

08:58.120 --> 08:59.247
Damn it.

09:01.040 --> 09:02.333
- Sit.
- Hey, sit.

09:02.416 --> 09:03.251
Okay.

09:08.464 --> 09:11.551
How exactly did you end up with debt?

09:11.634 --> 09:14.637
A bunch of thugs got him. Smile Capital.

09:15.221 --> 09:18.057
Smile Capital? Those guys in Gwangan-dong?

09:18.683 --> 09:20.101
I don't know the location.

09:20.893 --> 09:22.228
Jeez.

09:23.145 --> 09:26.023
Hey, Smile Capital isn't just
a bunch of goons.

09:26.107 --> 09:27.608
They are a huge company.

09:28.109 --> 09:29.360
How much do you owe?

09:29.944 --> 09:32.071
- A hundred million won.
- Jeez.

09:35.908 --> 09:37.076
You're totally screwed.

09:37.159 --> 09:39.078
Exactly. So help us out.

09:39.161 --> 09:40.580
You have a lot of money.

09:44.166 --> 09:47.336
I'll give you a 1% interest loan
of 100 million for one year.

09:49.505 --> 09:51.007
Thank you so much.

09:53.134 --> 09:56.095
In exchange, I want you
to work for me like you used to.

09:56.178 --> 09:58.848
This industry is booming,
thanks to COVID-19.

09:58.931 --> 10:01.183
Let's strike while the iron's hot
and make money.

10:01.767 --> 10:03.060
Help me out.

10:03.144 --> 10:06.480
I'll give you a fat bonus
on every collection you make.

10:08.149 --> 10:10.443
Jeez. This is a bit sudden.

10:10.526 --> 10:11.652
Damn it.

10:11.736 --> 10:14.155
Work as a bloodhound with me for a year.

10:15.072 --> 10:17.283
Hey, this is an opportunity.

10:17.366 --> 10:19.827
It's an opportunity to make big money.

10:20.328 --> 10:22.622
When would you ever
get to make this much money?

10:23.122 --> 10:26.500
I know what you mean,
but this is so sudden…

10:27.627 --> 10:29.462
- Make up your mind.
- Let's go.

10:31.213 --> 10:32.048
What?

10:32.131 --> 10:34.383
Don't these runs involve beating people?

10:36.469 --> 10:39.305
If you prey on the weak for money,
that makes you a thug.

10:40.473 --> 10:41.390
We're boxers.

10:44.018 --> 10:44.977
Hey, kiddo.

10:45.645 --> 10:48.564
If you don't pay back Smile Capital,
you're going to die.

10:48.648 --> 10:50.274
They'll even take your organs.

11:02.536 --> 11:03.579
What are you doing?

11:03.663 --> 11:07.083
Thank you for everything.
I'll come by some other time.

11:08.209 --> 11:09.043
Hey, let's go.

11:09.835 --> 11:11.504
Are you fucking with me?

11:14.048 --> 11:15.216
Does it look like I am?

11:24.725 --> 11:26.018
I'm just kidding.

11:27.520 --> 11:28.688
See you again.

11:31.524 --> 11:32.483
Hey, let's go.

11:35.903 --> 11:37.905
Fuck.

11:39.365 --> 11:40.366
Hey, boxer.

11:47.039 --> 11:48.874
- Stamp it.
- Okay.

11:50.167 --> 11:53.462
Once your business takes off,
make sure to give us a cut too, okay?

11:53.546 --> 11:56.132
Thank you so much.

12:01.470 --> 12:02.930
- Great work, sir.
- Let's go.

13:11.957 --> 13:12.958
There's no problem, right?

13:13.459 --> 13:14.627
No, sir.

13:15.127 --> 13:17.338
Right. Here.

13:17.421 --> 13:19.590
Here's the money we collected today.

13:20.966 --> 13:25.596
We are going around
gathering IDs from homeless people.

13:25.679 --> 13:27.181
Who are you?

13:27.264 --> 13:29.433
What are you looking at?
Get back to your work.

13:29.517 --> 13:30.434
Okay.

13:31.894 --> 13:36.524
We will work hard to get you the amount
you require as soon as possible.

13:39.693 --> 13:41.237
Can you get it done this week?

13:41.320 --> 13:43.322
This week? I'll try, sir.

13:43.405 --> 13:46.075
KIM JUN-MIN

13:49.870 --> 13:51.664
MASKS ARE REQUIRED
IN THE WAITING ROOM

13:56.627 --> 13:59.713
I hope I didn't keep you
waiting for too long.

14:02.675 --> 14:04.760
Why aren't you wearing your mask?

14:05.511 --> 14:06.345
I'll wear it.

14:06.428 --> 14:10.182
No, I'm not telling you to put it back on.
I asked you why you took it off.

14:10.266 --> 14:12.434
You kept us waiting for over 30 minutes.

14:12.518 --> 14:13.519
It was too stuffy.

14:13.602 --> 14:17.523
Punk! How do you expect to protect people
when you have no patience?

14:17.606 --> 14:20.818
What does wearing a mask
have to do with protecting people?

14:20.901 --> 14:21.735
Get out.

14:22.945 --> 14:23.779
Leave!

14:26.073 --> 14:26.949
Fuck.

14:29.410 --> 14:31.036
That bastard.

14:32.663 --> 14:33.831
Damn it.

14:35.833 --> 14:38.002
- You had your mask off, didn't you?
- No.

14:38.085 --> 14:38.919
I saw.

14:39.503 --> 14:40.796
I just had it pulled down.

14:40.880 --> 14:44.258
That's the same as taking it off.
Don't make an excuse, coward. Get out!

14:45.301 --> 14:46.135
I said, get out!

14:46.218 --> 14:47.928
Fuck.

14:49.305 --> 14:51.307
"Fuck"?

14:51.807 --> 14:53.893
"Fuck"?

14:53.976 --> 14:55.394
Jeez.

14:58.606 --> 14:59.648
Pull down your mask.

15:03.777 --> 15:05.112
What is your name?

15:05.696 --> 15:06.780
Cheon Dong-woo, sir.

15:06.864 --> 15:08.198
I see. What's your height?

15:08.282 --> 15:10.242
I'm 187 centimeters and 74 kilograms.

15:10.910 --> 15:11.869
Any training?

15:11.952 --> 15:14.288
I've done ten years
of kickboxing and hapkido.

15:14.371 --> 15:17.499
- What's your major?
- Security Services at Yongheon University.

15:20.294 --> 15:23.255
Wow. You're a total elite.

15:23.339 --> 15:24.298
Any military service?

15:24.381 --> 15:25.299
I was exempt.

15:26.383 --> 15:28.427
I tore my ACL
while playing foot volleyball.

15:29.428 --> 15:30.262
I see.

15:32.014 --> 15:32.848
See you next time.

15:32.932 --> 15:34.767
May I ask why you're turning me down?

15:35.517 --> 15:36.727
I'm looking for a Marine.

15:36.810 --> 15:38.228
Does it have to be a Marine?

15:38.312 --> 15:40.147
Yes.

15:40.648 --> 15:44.193
Damn it. Then you should've mentioned that
in your job post.

15:44.276 --> 15:46.362
Hold up. "Damn it"?

15:46.445 --> 15:48.447
You just wasted my time!

15:48.530 --> 15:50.991
That's not the way
to behave in front of your elder.

15:51.075 --> 15:52.284
Screw that.

15:52.368 --> 15:54.745
As a fucking elder,
you shouldn't screw around like that--

15:58.374 --> 16:00.167
I'll see you next time, okay?

16:00.751 --> 16:01.585
Yes, sir!

16:04.129 --> 16:07.049
MARINE
IF IT DOESN'T WORK, MAKE IT WORK!

16:11.220 --> 16:13.138
1216TH CLASS HONG WOO-JIN

16:23.315 --> 16:24.274
Get over here.

16:25.734 --> 16:26.902
Why are we running?

16:26.986 --> 16:28.529
He was in the 734th class!

16:31.865 --> 16:35.536
There is only one man in Korea
who can move a trillion in cash

16:35.619 --> 16:37.579
with just one phone call.

16:38.330 --> 16:39.540
Chairman Bang Seong-ho.

16:41.667 --> 16:45.004
And there's only one person
who knows what Chairman Bang looks like.

16:45.087 --> 16:46.797
There's always one person
for each situation.

16:46.880 --> 16:48.424
Keep quiet.

16:49.341 --> 16:52.553
Chairman Bang only trusted
and offered his tutelage to one person.

16:52.636 --> 16:54.096
That person is Mr. Choi.

16:54.179 --> 16:58.600
And Mr. Choi is the reason
I'm able to make a living in this field.

16:58.684 --> 17:01.103
You understand this universe now, right?

17:01.186 --> 17:02.229
- Well, yes.
- Yes.

17:02.312 --> 17:04.523
All right. I like that.

17:05.024 --> 17:07.776
Mr. Choi is currently looking
to hire someone.

17:07.860 --> 17:11.363
Someone willing to risk their lives
in any situation to save a person.

17:11.864 --> 17:13.198
Someone respectable.

17:13.282 --> 17:17.286
Someone somewhat knowledgeable
about our line of work.

17:17.369 --> 17:21.623
Yesterday, I started going through
some applicants,

17:21.707 --> 17:23.834
but they all fell short.

17:23.917 --> 17:27.796
During that time,
a junior Marine called me.

17:27.880 --> 17:29.715
Talk about impeccable timing!

17:31.091 --> 17:33.677
My friend here is a Marine too.
He's a senior Marine.

17:34.261 --> 17:35.137
What class are you?

17:35.220 --> 17:36.722
The 1207th, sir.

17:36.805 --> 17:38.974
I'm the 734th.

17:40.267 --> 17:43.437
- You see that?
- Man, I like what I see!

17:43.520 --> 17:46.607
I will put in a good word
about you two to Mr. Choi.

17:47.691 --> 17:49.193
So put down your ID numbers here.

17:49.693 --> 17:50.527
Well, sir.

17:51.987 --> 17:55.699
We actually contacted you
because we need a loan.

17:56.325 --> 17:59.536
That's why I'm telling you
to go meet Mr. Choi.

17:59.620 --> 18:01.705
He can be scary as a tiger,

18:01.789 --> 18:04.792
but he has the deepest
and most understanding heart.

18:04.875 --> 18:06.835
Once he accepts you as one of his own,

18:06.919 --> 18:09.296
he will always take care of you
like a true Marine!

18:10.005 --> 18:11.340
Is he a senior Marine?

18:12.758 --> 18:14.343
Are you asking if he's a Marine?

18:14.426 --> 18:15.511
Yes.

18:17.387 --> 18:20.140
He got an exemption
for dropping out of middle school.

18:21.517 --> 18:23.685
I see. It was a figure of speech.

18:23.769 --> 18:27.981
Kind of like how rappers say,
"This is hip hop. That is hip hop." Right?

18:30.567 --> 18:33.987
What are you talking about?
Just write down your ID numbers!

18:34.613 --> 18:35.447
Yes, sir.

18:42.412 --> 18:43.539
I saw the look on his face.

18:43.622 --> 18:45.707
- Yes.
- I think things will work out.

18:46.291 --> 18:47.668
- Thank you.
- Let's go.

18:47.751 --> 18:49.461
There's nothing to thank me for.

18:50.337 --> 18:52.464
Anyway, how many did you fight?

18:53.549 --> 18:54.550
Maybe around ten?

18:55.592 --> 18:56.969
But one guy took me down.

18:57.469 --> 18:58.303
Just one?

18:58.804 --> 19:02.182
He was built like a tank.
He grabbed me and headbutted me.

19:02.266 --> 19:04.601
There's not much
you can do about headbutts.

19:06.812 --> 19:08.564
Hey. What if

19:09.523 --> 19:12.651
you have to work as a debt collector
to pay off your mom's loans?

19:12.734 --> 19:13.652
What will you do?

19:19.491 --> 19:21.201
Let's think about it together.

19:34.631 --> 19:36.008
Excellent work, as usual.

19:36.592 --> 19:37.885
Thank you.

19:38.385 --> 19:41.430
No, we will take care of that.

19:41.513 --> 19:43.724
That is Mr. Oh's specialty.

19:44.266 --> 19:45.392
All right.

19:45.475 --> 19:49.188
Let's eat at Yang-jung's place
sometime soon.

19:49.271 --> 19:50.189
See you.

19:53.275 --> 19:56.528
Yang Jae-myeong went
to Chungjeong-ro and Myeong-dong

19:56.612 --> 19:59.573
to take out 400 million in cash
from seven different loan sharks.

20:00.240 --> 20:03.911
He then gave it to a director who works
for Smile Capital in Gwangan-dong.

20:04.912 --> 20:05.787
Do you know him?

20:07.331 --> 20:08.916
I don't know him.

20:08.999 --> 20:11.293
Yang Jae-myeong is stealing
identities of the homeless

20:11.376 --> 20:12.961
to create shell corporations,

20:13.545 --> 20:15.547
and he's borrowing money from loan sharks.

20:15.631 --> 20:18.217
Loan sharks fall for it
since they don't share information

20:18.300 --> 20:21.511
with each other, and they don't have
any knowledge of this trick.

20:22.095 --> 20:25.349
So they find out when they go
to the fake company to collect the money.

20:25.849 --> 20:29.061
This was plotted by someone
who is well-versed in how cash flows.

20:29.561 --> 20:32.814
Looks like Yang Jae-myeong is just a pawn.

20:33.732 --> 20:35.359
How do you know about this?

20:35.943 --> 20:38.362
Was it the year 2001? Or was it 2002?

20:38.445 --> 20:41.573
A guy pretending to volunteer
at a facility for the disabled

20:41.657 --> 20:44.034
stole a bunch of IDs.

20:44.534 --> 20:47.329
He created a paper company
and used it to take out a loan

20:47.412 --> 20:52.000
worth seven billion won
from loan sharks in Myeong-dong

20:52.084 --> 20:53.919
and ran off to the Philippines.

20:54.419 --> 20:56.088
That's worth tens of billions today.

20:57.631 --> 20:59.132
What are we going to do?

20:59.216 --> 21:00.384
What?

21:00.467 --> 21:03.136
Those loan sharks are getting conned.

21:03.220 --> 21:04.930
In a way, they're your juniors.

21:05.013 --> 21:06.848
I'm sure they'll manage well themselves.

21:07.432 --> 21:10.185
Loan sharks can't exactly go to the cops.

21:11.103 --> 21:15.148
Hyeon-ju, this is something
they should solve by themselves.

21:16.483 --> 21:19.444
I am someone that is dead to this world.

21:20.028 --> 21:21.571
I lived that way for ten years.

21:23.031 --> 21:26.326
So, what happened to that person
who went to the Philippines?

21:26.410 --> 21:27.244
Did he get caught?

21:27.327 --> 21:29.371
The people who lost money to him

21:29.454 --> 21:32.124
sent bloodhounds to the Philippines.

21:32.624 --> 21:33.583
Did he die?

21:37.713 --> 21:39.172
That's brutal.

21:39.715 --> 21:40.882
Hyeon-ju.

21:40.966 --> 21:43.510
Should I hire someone
to help with your work?

21:44.094 --> 21:45.595
Well, no.

21:45.679 --> 21:48.473
It's dangerous, and you even got hurt.

21:48.557 --> 21:50.309
It's just a scratch.

21:50.392 --> 21:51.268
Still.

21:51.351 --> 21:53.895
It's faster and easier
for me to work alone.

21:53.979 --> 21:55.063
Get some sleep.

21:56.815 --> 21:57.733
Hey, you brat!

22:02.154 --> 22:03.071
Nice shot!

22:04.197 --> 22:07.242
Sir, why did you do that to a kid's face?

22:14.291 --> 22:15.500
Who told you?

22:15.584 --> 22:17.627
I asked In-beom.

22:18.420 --> 22:19.838
Beom talks about these things?

22:20.714 --> 22:23.091
- He does to me.
- Let me finish this one.

22:27.262 --> 22:28.138
Nice.

22:32.517 --> 22:35.103
He spat on my face in front of the boys.

22:36.813 --> 22:38.482
I was setting an example.

22:39.858 --> 22:41.943
If you get involved,
it's more work for me.

22:47.199 --> 22:48.158
Jang-do.

22:49.242 --> 22:51.661
You need to step forward
and take action sometimes.

22:51.745 --> 22:53.497
That is how they fear you.

22:54.664 --> 22:55.499
Yes, sir.

22:57.459 --> 22:59.878
Anyway, why hasn't this rich kid
contacted me yet?

22:59.961 --> 23:01.338
It's been over a week.

23:01.838 --> 23:04.299
I'll talk to Mr. Park
and set up a meeting soon.

23:04.383 --> 23:05.634
One meeting is all we need.

23:06.343 --> 23:07.177
Let's do that.

23:25.112 --> 23:26.446
38TH NATIONAL ROOKIE APPLICATION

23:28.615 --> 23:31.785
Wow, he really built quite the physique.

23:31.868 --> 23:34.746
Didn't you box back in the day too, sir?

23:34.830 --> 23:37.165
I was just an amateur.

23:37.833 --> 23:40.961
This body alone tells a story
of diligence and spirit.

23:41.044 --> 23:43.296
Bodies don't lie.

23:43.380 --> 23:44.589
That is true, sir.

23:45.215 --> 23:49.302
But that kid doesn't know a thing
about the loan business.

23:51.847 --> 23:52.722
Thank you.

23:52.806 --> 23:55.892
He's the kid who's been hanging out
with Kim Gun-woo these days.

23:55.976 --> 23:57.436
According to a detective agency,

23:58.520 --> 24:01.398
he has beaten up a bunch
of gang members in Incheon

24:01.481 --> 24:03.567
and joined the Marine Corps
to hide from them.

24:04.067 --> 24:05.777
He's lived diligently
since being discharged.

24:05.861 --> 24:09.489
He went on some runs,
so he should know the basics.

24:10.615 --> 24:13.785
I think it might be good
to hire both of them.

24:15.704 --> 24:18.665
- Let me see Gun-woo for now.
- Yes, sir.

24:19.458 --> 24:20.292
There it is.

24:24.171 --> 24:26.047
SUSHI

24:31.470 --> 24:32.429
Hello, sir.

24:32.512 --> 24:33.346
Hello.

24:34.473 --> 24:36.308
You were introduced by Mr. Moon, right?

24:36.391 --> 24:37.350
Yes.

24:39.394 --> 24:40.437
This way, please.

24:47.027 --> 24:48.320
- Go ahead.
- Me?

24:48.820 --> 24:49.654
Yes.

25:28.693 --> 25:30.612
Hello, I am Kim Gun-woo.

25:31.947 --> 25:32.781
Please sit.

25:32.864 --> 25:33.698
Yes, sir.

25:42.415 --> 25:44.751
May I speak freely?

25:45.627 --> 25:46.461
Yes, sir.

25:52.592 --> 25:54.344
Did you hurt your face?

25:54.928 --> 25:59.349
I got hurt trying to stop the loan sharks
who were destroying my mother's café.

26:02.143 --> 26:04.312
I was once a loan shark myself.

26:06.398 --> 26:08.900
It has been a while since I quit.

26:09.484 --> 26:10.360
Yes, sir.

26:10.443 --> 26:14.030
Now, I am in the business
of offering zero-interest loans

26:15.156 --> 26:17.409
to sick people who can't afford treatment.

26:17.993 --> 26:18.827
I see.

26:21.871 --> 26:23.456
I am looking for a person.

26:24.833 --> 26:28.295
There's a young kid
who's learning the business from me.

26:28.962 --> 26:30.046
I see.

26:30.130 --> 26:31.923
We're not related by blood.

26:33.466 --> 26:35.093
That kid's the only family I have.

26:35.677 --> 26:36.720
Yes, sir.

26:36.803 --> 26:40.599
I worry that she might get hurt
while getting around alone.

26:41.891 --> 26:46.313
So I was hoping for a good person
to be by her side and keep her safe.

26:48.565 --> 26:50.275
It's not debt collection, right?

26:50.358 --> 26:52.819
No, it's not debt collection.

26:54.487 --> 26:57.449
- It's personal security.
- I see. Yes!

27:00.243 --> 27:03.038
You might find it offensive,

27:03.788 --> 27:05.915
but I've done a little digging on you.

27:05.999 --> 27:08.001
Not at all. I'm not offended at all.

27:08.084 --> 27:11.546
I heard that even in hardship,
you didn't lose the goodness in you

27:12.547 --> 27:14.507
and that you've lived a diligent life.

27:14.591 --> 27:16.926
Seeing you in person like this,

27:17.010 --> 27:18.720
I see you have a strong gaze.

27:21.973 --> 27:22.974
You seem trustworthy.

27:23.058 --> 27:24.184
Thank you.

27:29.356 --> 27:30.190
Well…

27:32.734 --> 27:34.235
Why did you start boxing?

27:34.819 --> 27:36.446
I wanted to get stronger when I was a kid.

27:37.030 --> 27:37.864
Why?

27:38.740 --> 27:41.368
My father wasn't much of a drinker.

27:42.369 --> 27:44.996
Things became difficult
in my first year of middle school.

27:45.080 --> 27:47.540
He began drinking and hitting my mom.

27:48.124 --> 27:51.294
Seeing that when I was a child
made me want to get stronger.

27:54.089 --> 27:56.466
- Does he live with you?
- No, well…

27:57.008 --> 28:00.387
They got divorced when I was 16.
I haven't seen him since.

28:01.513 --> 28:03.932
- I'm from the countryside.
- I see.

28:04.015 --> 28:07.394
My father was a tenant farmer.

28:07.477 --> 28:08.353
I see.

28:09.104 --> 28:13.191
I remember very vividly when I was ten.

28:13.775 --> 28:16.986
There was a severe famine,
resulting in abysmal yields for the year.

28:17.070 --> 28:18.988
When we failed to pay rent,

28:19.614 --> 28:21.950
the landlord got his servants

28:23.034 --> 28:24.911
to brutally beat up my father…

28:27.414 --> 28:29.582
in front of the villagers.

28:30.750 --> 28:33.795
My father hurt his head badly,

28:33.878 --> 28:36.506
but we had no money to go to the hospital.

28:38.258 --> 28:40.427
He died after suffering at home.

28:41.094 --> 28:44.347
That's why I became determined
to make money.

28:44.931 --> 28:48.017
I decided to help those

28:49.519 --> 28:51.563
who could not afford treatment.

28:58.737 --> 29:02.866
I'm saying that we should overcome

29:02.949 --> 29:06.369
any difficult situation with a good heart.

29:06.453 --> 29:09.831
Yes, I always have a good heart.

29:15.879 --> 29:17.297
Our conversation isn't flowing.

29:17.380 --> 29:20.800
Yes, I'm sorry.
I'm not very good with words.

29:20.884 --> 29:23.052
- Is that so?
- Yes, sir.

29:28.099 --> 29:29.601
- Come over here.
- Okay.

29:31.311 --> 29:32.145
How did it go?

29:33.605 --> 29:34.814
I think I did well.

29:35.315 --> 29:37.901
Mr. Choi talked a lot,
so I mostly listened.

29:37.984 --> 29:40.528
I told you it would go well!

29:42.238 --> 29:43.239
Hey.

29:44.407 --> 29:45.658
How was it?

29:46.242 --> 29:48.620
Well, the kid is certainly no fun…

29:51.456 --> 29:52.582
but he's a good kid.

29:54.918 --> 29:55.752
I see.

29:59.839 --> 30:00.924
Watch your step.

30:03.259 --> 30:04.928
It seems he needs money urgently.

30:05.011 --> 30:07.597
- Please take care of it today.
- Yes, sir.

30:08.890 --> 30:10.683
- Give me a little.
- Eat a lot, Woo-jin.

30:10.767 --> 30:11.976
It's a bit much.

30:17.273 --> 30:19.192
There's not much, but please enjoy.

30:19.275 --> 30:22.153
Ma'am, I love kimchi stew.

30:22.237 --> 30:23.571
May I try it?

30:23.655 --> 30:24.739
Yes, go ahead.

30:27.826 --> 30:28.660
Be careful. It's hot.

30:28.743 --> 30:30.995
It's so good. Thank you for this meal.

30:31.079 --> 30:32.747
Yes, please enjoy.

30:34.082 --> 30:39.003
Well, we really appreciate your help
with this.

30:39.087 --> 30:42.465
Don't mention it.
Gun-woo is a dear friend of mine.

30:43.550 --> 30:44.926
Besides, Marines, "Ack!"

30:45.510 --> 30:47.178
Everything will work out fine.

30:48.680 --> 30:49.806
Thank you.

30:49.889 --> 30:51.307
Please dig in.

30:51.391 --> 30:53.059
- Yes, ma'am!
- Thank you for cooking.

30:53.142 --> 30:53.977
Sure, eat up.

30:56.062 --> 30:56.896
Who's that?

30:58.314 --> 30:59.774
- I'll go see who it is.
- Okay.

31:00.275 --> 31:01.359
Who is it?

31:04.445 --> 31:06.114
Hello, how can I help you?

31:06.197 --> 31:08.074
I work for Mr. Choi.

31:08.825 --> 31:09.742
I see.

31:13.162 --> 31:14.455
Nice to meet you.

31:14.539 --> 31:16.749
Here. It's a hundred million won.

31:17.333 --> 31:20.461
- What?
- It's two years' pay in advance.

31:22.672 --> 31:23.590
I mean…

31:31.014 --> 31:32.932
Work starts at 10:00 a.m. tomorrow.

31:33.016 --> 31:35.643
I will text you the office address.

31:40.148 --> 31:43.526
Thank you, sir. Thank you so much.

31:44.527 --> 31:46.863
You should thank Mr. Choi.

31:46.946 --> 31:48.197
- Yes.
- I'll get going.

31:49.157 --> 31:50.700
Thank you so much.

32:17.644 --> 32:19.437
These rolled omelets are delicious.

32:20.063 --> 32:21.439
I will cook you more.

32:24.108 --> 32:25.109
Who was it?

32:27.612 --> 32:28.446
Here…

32:31.824 --> 32:34.077
Mom, the thing is,

32:34.160 --> 32:37.413
I got a job
through an acquaintance of Woo-jin.

32:37.497 --> 32:38.414
What kind of work?

32:38.998 --> 32:43.378
I'll be a bodyguard for a family member
of a rich businessman.

32:44.545 --> 32:46.881
He thought highly of me,

32:46.965 --> 32:50.301
so he gave me 100 million won
as an advance on two years' worth of work.

32:54.138 --> 32:55.932
- Really?
- Yes.

32:56.015 --> 33:00.311
Let's use this to pay off our debt first,
so it doesn't accrue interest.

33:08.695 --> 33:11.531
I feel like I've ruined your future.

33:12.824 --> 33:14.492
No, you didn't…

33:16.202 --> 33:19.497
Living happily with you
matters more than anything to me.

33:19.580 --> 33:21.290
I can train hard while working.

33:21.374 --> 33:24.210
I'll start boxing again
once the pandemic is over. It's okay.

33:26.629 --> 33:28.464
I'm so sorry.

33:33.720 --> 33:37.056
Let's smile, okay? This is a good thing.

33:45.273 --> 33:46.441
Thanks, Woo-jin.

34:08.337 --> 34:09.797
- Hello, sir.
- Get out of the way.

34:09.881 --> 34:11.007
Myeong-gil, come here.

34:12.967 --> 34:13.801
What is it?

34:14.635 --> 34:16.012
He arrived 20 minutes ago.

34:16.095 --> 34:16.929
He's early.

34:17.013 --> 34:19.182
He's the eldest son
of lil Group's chairman, right?

34:19.766 --> 34:22.727
- You know him?
- Myeong-gil, be careful with that guy.

34:23.311 --> 34:24.187
- Why?
- Over here!

34:24.270 --> 34:25.438
Yes, sir.

34:26.856 --> 34:28.066
Get me some wet wipes.

34:28.149 --> 34:30.401
I pressed the bell, but no one came.

34:30.485 --> 34:32.570
I'm sorry, sir.
I will get you some right away.

34:32.653 --> 34:34.739
When I worked at Speed
as an assistant manager,

34:34.822 --> 34:36.657
he had some drinks and fought the owner.

34:36.741 --> 34:38.993
- You mean Hyeon-ji?
- Yes.

34:39.077 --> 34:41.662
They had an argument
talking politics over drinks.

34:41.746 --> 34:45.166
A few days later, the store was subjected
to a tax investigation.

34:45.750 --> 34:48.294
She had to sell off her house
to pay off the taxes.

34:48.795 --> 34:52.090
We found out later that his family
has connections everywhere.

34:52.173 --> 34:54.967
National Tax Service, Police Agency,
Financial Supervisory Service…

34:55.468 --> 34:56.761
His family is everywhere.

34:56.844 --> 34:58.554
The chaebol are like that.

34:59.263 --> 35:00.098
Really?

35:00.598 --> 35:03.059
The politician Hyeon-ji cursed at
could be his family.

35:03.142 --> 35:04.644
I see.

35:05.520 --> 35:07.730
I was just worried about you.

35:09.232 --> 35:10.149
All right.

35:10.942 --> 35:12.527
Did you arrange some pretty girls?

35:13.444 --> 35:14.946
He told us not to.

35:17.990 --> 35:19.700
All right. Don't worry, okay?

35:21.994 --> 35:23.287
He brought someone with him.

35:23.371 --> 35:25.331
- Who?
- A senior from the Police Academy.

35:28.751 --> 35:29.919
Is he still active?

35:30.002 --> 35:32.421
Yes. He graduated top of his class.

35:35.341 --> 35:36.342
Does he know you?

35:37.844 --> 35:40.221
I don't think so.
There are several years between us.

35:46.727 --> 35:48.396
No matter what happens, stand down.

35:48.980 --> 35:51.107
- Understood?
- Yes, sir.

35:55.236 --> 35:57.155
- I will ask them to put in a call.
- Okay.

36:00.825 --> 36:01.784
Hello, sir.

36:02.493 --> 36:03.452
You're here.

36:04.662 --> 36:07.540
He is a cousin of mine.

36:07.623 --> 36:09.584
I'm Min Gang-yong. Nice to meet you.

36:09.667 --> 36:11.294
You have a great voice.

36:11.377 --> 36:12.587
I am Kim Myeong-gil.

36:12.670 --> 36:15.339
He said he had hard liquor,
so I shamelessly joined.

36:15.423 --> 36:16.424
I hope you don't mind.

36:16.507 --> 36:19.886
I heard you're a man who does big things.
It's an honor to meet you.

36:19.969 --> 36:21.095
The honor is all mine.

36:21.971 --> 36:24.724
This is Lee Jin-su, an associate of mine.

36:25.308 --> 36:28.603
I see. We've met before, haven't we?

36:28.686 --> 36:30.521
I do have a rather common face.

36:31.189 --> 36:32.023
I must apologize.

36:33.191 --> 36:34.025
Have a seat.

36:34.108 --> 36:34.942
Sure.

36:37.695 --> 36:40.531
I didn't want to drink on your dime,
so I brought my own.

36:41.157 --> 36:42.450
I wanted to treat you today.

36:46.495 --> 36:47.371
Let me.

36:52.793 --> 36:55.046
I apologize on his behalf.
He does not drink.

36:55.129 --> 36:58.174
You being the only sober one
would complicate things.

36:58.257 --> 37:02.595
Getting drunk together guarantees
that no one changes their mind later on.

37:02.678 --> 37:05.890
Then why don't you drink his share too,
as a loyal friend would?

37:05.973 --> 37:07.225
You seem like a drinker.

37:07.308 --> 37:08.684
I like loyalty.

37:10.269 --> 37:11.562
Sure, pour me a glass.

37:25.576 --> 37:27.078
Look at you gulp it down.

37:27.787 --> 37:28.829
It's smooth, right?

37:29.538 --> 37:30.414
It is.

37:30.915 --> 37:32.416
Now allow me.

37:33.834 --> 37:35.002
Would you like a shot?

37:35.920 --> 37:38.130
I think you had a bigger glass in mind.

37:38.214 --> 37:40.007
- I'll take that.
- Sure.

37:42.593 --> 37:43.928
Jeez.

37:44.011 --> 37:45.888
Government employees usually drink soju.

37:45.972 --> 37:49.809
But to drink some Blue in a glass…
I guess today is my lucky day.

37:57.233 --> 37:58.484
Now a glass from me.

38:26.929 --> 38:28.472
You drink well.

38:29.056 --> 38:31.976
I'd also like a glass.
It's my liquor, after all.

38:32.852 --> 38:33.686
Yes?

38:34.312 --> 38:35.896
Sure. I'll pour it with one hand.

38:41.193 --> 38:42.111
Go ahead.

38:56.667 --> 38:57.752
Here.

39:04.800 --> 39:05.801
Wow.

39:07.011 --> 39:07.845
Now!

39:09.430 --> 39:10.264
Bottoms up!

39:24.779 --> 39:26.614
You both drink very well.

39:26.697 --> 39:30.284
Gang-yong, if I get drunk
and do something stupid, please stop me.

39:30.368 --> 39:31.994
Okay. If things get out of hand…

39:32.078 --> 39:33.746
Where is it? I will…

39:38.250 --> 39:39.502
arrest someone.

39:46.008 --> 39:47.176
Gather your glasses.

40:04.777 --> 40:05.736
Fuck.

40:07.113 --> 40:12.118
Now that we've shared some drinks,
why don't we lay it all out on the table?

40:13.119 --> 40:14.036
Let's do that.

40:15.830 --> 40:16.747
Are you rich?

40:16.831 --> 40:19.417
I come from a humble background,
so I'm working hard.

40:21.127 --> 40:22.211
Do you have 100 billion?

40:23.421 --> 40:26.590
I don't lie about money matters.

40:26.674 --> 40:28.259
Is that so?

40:29.802 --> 40:31.220
That's odd.

40:31.303 --> 40:34.807
I was told that we could comb through
every nook and cranny of Smile Capital

40:35.307 --> 40:36.934
but wouldn't even find 50 billion.

40:37.017 --> 40:38.561
You're right.

40:38.644 --> 40:41.439
I guess the National Tax Agency
isn't doing its job right.

40:41.522 --> 40:42.731
Shall we call them?

40:43.691 --> 40:45.151
Jeez, you're drunk.

40:45.234 --> 40:47.945
Mr. Kim doesn't look too happy.
Hurry up and apologize.

40:48.571 --> 40:49.655
Right. I'm sorry.

40:50.239 --> 40:54.785
I drank too much on an empty stomach.
The alcohol is hitting me really hard.

40:55.369 --> 40:57.538
You don't need to worry about the money.

40:59.123 --> 41:00.207
Is that right?

41:00.875 --> 41:01.917
I see.

41:02.877 --> 41:05.629
I guess I should never worry about money.

41:08.257 --> 41:12.136
By the way, my mom asked me
to send my regards to Chairman Bang.

41:12.970 --> 41:14.513
She is thankful for back then.

41:16.056 --> 41:18.601
But the person who got her
the money that day…

41:22.229 --> 41:24.356
was apparently in his mid-forties.

41:25.483 --> 41:29.570
How is it that you have remained
in your mid-forties for twenty years?

41:30.696 --> 41:31.947
Was it plastic surgery?

41:33.574 --> 41:35.117
It's really common nowadays.

41:38.704 --> 41:41.749
I guess you thought
I wouldn't ask my mom, right?

41:41.832 --> 41:43.250
What is going on?

41:43.334 --> 41:44.877
Why so quiet?

41:45.503 --> 41:49.548
Hello? Are you the type to just shut
your mouth when you're at a disadvantage?

41:52.468 --> 41:54.678
Is that what they taught you
back in prison?

41:58.057 --> 41:59.642
Man, this guy is laughing.

41:59.725 --> 42:01.852
All right, smile.

42:03.479 --> 42:05.648
Damn it, Gang-yong!

42:06.273 --> 42:09.443
I don't feel like drinking anymore.
Let's wrap it up.

42:10.569 --> 42:11.612
Mr. Kim.

42:12.238 --> 42:13.989
I came up with the 100 billion won.

42:14.740 --> 42:17.034
So we'll never cross paths again.

42:19.078 --> 42:20.162
Come here, Kimmie.

42:22.289 --> 42:23.624
Come on, hurry.

42:34.426 --> 42:35.678
If you mess around

42:36.262 --> 42:38.347
with my family name again,

42:40.182 --> 42:41.392
you'll die.

42:47.439 --> 42:48.315
Got it?

42:49.316 --> 42:50.150
Yes?

42:52.444 --> 42:56.198
You did live a diligent life!
You even have a knife wound here.

42:56.282 --> 42:57.741
What did I tell you?

42:57.825 --> 42:58.826
Hey, let's go.

42:58.909 --> 43:01.453
Let's go. We were here for so damn long.

43:01.537 --> 43:04.415
Mr. Kim, I tried to give you
the benefit of the doubt.

43:04.498 --> 43:06.792
You looked like a hard-working guy.

43:19.305 --> 43:20.139
Jang-do.

43:20.639 --> 43:21.473
Yes, sir.

43:22.891 --> 43:25.978
Go with Beom and find something
to use against that guy.

43:26.478 --> 43:27.646
Something big.

43:29.690 --> 43:30.524
Understood, sir.

43:31.025 --> 43:33.944
ANTIQUES SHOPPING CENTER

43:41.452 --> 43:43.621
- Thanks for coming with me.
- No problem.

43:46.540 --> 43:47.374
What is it?

43:48.459 --> 43:49.460
What?

43:49.543 --> 43:51.795
- Are you coming in too?
- Yes.

43:51.879 --> 43:54.965
I figured I might make my case
to Mr. Choi and get a job too.

43:55.049 --> 43:55.966
Don't you want that?

43:56.050 --> 43:57.760
I would totally love that.

43:57.843 --> 43:59.970
Right? So back me up
when I'm talking to him.

44:00.054 --> 44:01.472
Make me look good.

44:01.555 --> 44:03.307
- Okay.
- All right. Let's go.

44:19.990 --> 44:21.367
BOOKS
PYEONGHWA BOOKS

44:25.704 --> 44:27.373
- Hello, sir!
- Hello, sir!

44:30.084 --> 44:31.126
You didn't get lost.

44:31.210 --> 44:32.169
No, sir.

44:32.670 --> 44:35.923
I used the money you gave me
to pay off my loans this morning.

44:36.006 --> 44:38.842
Thank you so much.

44:40.928 --> 44:42.805
I believe you will do well.

44:42.888 --> 44:44.348
I will do my best.

44:44.848 --> 44:48.185
Hello, sir! My name is Hong Woo-jin.

44:48.268 --> 44:50.896
I helped Mr. Moon
with his work back in the day.

44:51.397 --> 44:54.858
Gun-woo and I had a special relationship
in the Marine Corps.

44:54.942 --> 44:56.026
Yes.

44:56.110 --> 44:58.904
Watching Gun-woo's struggle
from the sidelines,

44:58.987 --> 45:02.408
I wanted to help in any way I could,
but there wasn't much I could do.

45:02.491 --> 45:04.993
And it ate me up inside.

45:05.077 --> 45:08.497
However, I'm so relieved
that a good person like you helped him.

45:08.580 --> 45:10.124
I'm just so grateful.

45:10.207 --> 45:12.167
Furthermore, I have come to the conclusion

45:12.251 --> 45:14.294
that I may be of service to you, sir.

45:14.378 --> 45:16.296
I'm better versed in this line of work.

45:17.631 --> 45:20.718
I'm embarrassed
to toot my own horn in front of you,

45:20.801 --> 45:23.178
the living legend of Myeong-dong,

45:23.762 --> 45:25.889
but I know the ropes
better than Gun-woo here.

45:25.973 --> 45:29.601
"Why don't I accompany Gun-woo
to show him the ropes

45:30.269 --> 45:31.353
and help him out"?

45:32.020 --> 45:34.356
"I mean, wouldn't this
help him out a little?"

45:34.440 --> 45:36.650
"No, it might work out greatly
in his favor."

45:36.734 --> 45:39.278
Those thoughts made me
take the liberty to come here.

45:39.862 --> 45:41.113
With your permission,

45:41.196 --> 45:43.323
I'd like to accompany Gun-woo
and help him!

45:50.873 --> 45:51.790
Sure, why not?

45:55.544 --> 45:56.462
Thank you, sir!

45:57.838 --> 45:58.797
Sit.

45:58.881 --> 45:59.798
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

46:02.342 --> 46:03.927
- Thank you!
- Thanks for the tea!

46:05.012 --> 46:07.431
There is one thing I didn't mention.

46:08.557 --> 46:11.727
I may be the one paying your salary,
but I'm not the one hiring you.

46:12.436 --> 46:13.270
Excuse me?

46:13.353 --> 46:15.564
You still have an interview with Hyeon-ju.

46:17.733 --> 46:18.942
I see.

46:19.026 --> 46:20.319
Well…

46:20.402 --> 46:23.030
What happens if I fail the interview?

46:23.113 --> 46:25.073
You would have to return the salary.

46:25.699 --> 46:30.245
Oh, I used it all to pay back our loans.

46:30.329 --> 46:32.080
I believe you will do well.

46:32.748 --> 46:33.582
What?

46:34.666 --> 46:39.463
Hyeon-ju is vehemently against
having a bodyguard though.

46:39.546 --> 46:42.633
But I am awful with words, Mr. Choi.

46:42.716 --> 46:43.926
Good luck.

46:44.009 --> 46:45.219
Mr. Choi.

46:45.302 --> 46:50.599
If I manage to persuade Hyeon-ju
to hire me and Gun-woo,

46:50.682 --> 46:52.351
can I also receive a salary?

46:55.354 --> 46:56.647
Let's do that.

46:56.730 --> 46:57.648
Woo-jin.

46:59.274 --> 47:01.485
I have a scalp massage I have to get to.

47:01.568 --> 47:02.861
- Yes.
- Bye now.

47:02.945 --> 47:04.571
Yes, sir. Enjoy your time.

47:04.655 --> 47:05.656
Right.

47:07.616 --> 47:08.784
Use this

47:09.535 --> 47:11.328
to get something nice for lunch.

47:13.121 --> 47:15.332
Okay. Thank you, sir.

47:16.792 --> 47:19.253
I really want to work
in this perfect company.

47:19.336 --> 47:20.170
Sir.

47:22.506 --> 47:23.841
You two…

47:26.552 --> 47:28.387
stick together, no matter what.

47:30.681 --> 47:31.598
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

47:32.099 --> 47:33.016
Godspeed!

47:33.100 --> 47:34.142
- Godspeed!
- Godspeed!

47:45.904 --> 47:46.738
What?

47:54.872 --> 47:55.831
Fuck!

47:57.124 --> 47:58.125
- What is it?
- Hey!

47:58.208 --> 47:59.334
What's this?

47:59.918 --> 48:02.296
- It was in here.
- Really?

48:02.796 --> 48:05.132
This has to be over a hundred million won.

48:05.215 --> 48:06.466
- A hundred million?
- Hey!

48:12.431 --> 48:13.307
Look at this.

48:14.933 --> 48:16.518
Jeez. It's in here too.

48:18.186 --> 48:19.104
Hold on a second.

48:38.415 --> 48:41.668
THERE WILL BE GUESTS AT THE BOOKSTORE
HAVE A NICE CHAT

48:42.461 --> 48:43.545
Damn it.

48:45.422 --> 48:47.716
17 billion, 18 billion,

48:48.467 --> 48:50.010
19 billion…

48:51.845 --> 48:53.931
- 21 billion, 22 billion…
- Woo-jin.

48:54.014 --> 48:55.140
To be honest,

48:56.350 --> 48:58.477
I have met Hyeon-ju before.

48:59.269 --> 49:01.480
What? What do you mean?

49:02.147 --> 49:04.316
When I went over
to see you a few days ago,

49:05.067 --> 49:07.694
a homeless person was being chased by her,

49:07.778 --> 49:11.031
so I followed her and got tased.

49:11.114 --> 49:13.283
- You got tased?
- Yes.

49:13.367 --> 49:15.577
Well, then, did you two fight?

49:15.661 --> 49:19.164
No, she just cursed at me. That's it.

49:19.247 --> 49:20.749
I see.

49:22.876 --> 49:23.877
Don't worry.

49:24.670 --> 49:26.296
I'll take care of everything.

49:26.380 --> 49:28.507
You just watch.

49:28.590 --> 49:30.801
Just keep your head down.

49:31.885 --> 49:33.595
I lost count because of you.

49:33.679 --> 49:34.554
Sorry.

49:44.815 --> 49:46.149
Hello, Ms. Hyeon-ju.

49:46.233 --> 49:49.486
We were hand-picked by Mr. Choi himself

49:49.569 --> 49:52.072
so that you can safely go about your work.

49:52.656 --> 49:56.743
Hashtag, bodyguard.
Hashtag, please be my security personnel.

49:56.827 --> 49:58.078
Hashtag, manager.

49:58.161 --> 50:02.374
Hashtag, your boys.

50:02.916 --> 50:04.501
What was that?

50:04.584 --> 50:07.713
Just think of us as your boys.
Nice to meet you.

50:10.799 --> 50:12.843
Just say the word.

50:12.926 --> 50:15.470
We will take care of anything you need.

50:15.554 --> 50:17.014
I do not need anything.

50:19.558 --> 50:21.601
Yes, so going forward,

50:21.685 --> 50:24.062
just tell us anything you need.

50:24.146 --> 50:27.107
No. I won't be needing anything
going forward, so leave.

50:33.155 --> 50:34.573
Do you not like us?

50:35.198 --> 50:37.492
How could I not like you
when we've just met?

50:37.576 --> 50:38.577
I just don't need you.

50:38.660 --> 50:41.830
You haven't seen us at work.
How do you know you don't need us?

50:42.497 --> 50:44.875
I had no problem
doing things alone until now,

50:44.958 --> 50:47.127
so I'm sure I don't need you.

50:47.627 --> 50:49.421
Plus, I hate people who argue.

50:49.504 --> 50:50.756
I'm not trying to argue--

50:50.839 --> 50:53.133
That's called arguing.

50:53.216 --> 50:54.593
Please leave.

51:01.099 --> 51:04.186
Mr. Choi said that we could stay.

51:05.103 --> 51:06.772
Weren't you trying to persuade me?

51:09.107 --> 51:12.277
You're starting to fucking lie now.

51:12.778 --> 51:14.905
I thought only your shoes were fake.

51:15.489 --> 51:16.531
Leave.

51:17.991 --> 51:19.284
I said get out!

51:20.869 --> 51:23.413
Hello, do you not hear me?

51:23.497 --> 51:25.791
Get the fuck out! Damn it!

51:45.102 --> 51:47.562
I really need this job.

51:47.646 --> 51:48.939
Use me for one month.

51:49.022 --> 51:51.441
If I'm no help, then I'll leave.

51:51.525 --> 51:53.777
Just a month, I'm begging you.

51:54.277 --> 51:55.237
Excuse me.

51:55.320 --> 51:58.448
If you need money,
my grandpa will lend you some.

51:58.949 --> 52:01.368
I'll put in a word for you, so leave.

52:01.451 --> 52:02.869
This is uncomfortable.

52:02.953 --> 52:03.870
The money…

52:05.747 --> 52:09.459
Mr. Choi gave me a two-year advance
on the pay already.

52:10.669 --> 52:13.922
My mom got duped by Smile Capital
and took out a loan.

52:14.714 --> 52:16.716
The debt snowballed to 100 million,

52:17.217 --> 52:20.470
so I had to pay it back this morning
with the money Mr. Choi gave me.

52:20.554 --> 52:25.016
If I have to return the money,
I will be in deep trouble.

52:25.517 --> 52:28.854
Please, I am begging you.

52:31.481 --> 52:32.774
Get up.

52:33.358 --> 52:34.276
Let's go eat.

52:44.035 --> 52:46.663
Why did you borrow money
from Smile Capital?

52:47.581 --> 52:48.915
My mom got conned.

52:50.625 --> 52:52.294
How big was the loan?

52:53.503 --> 52:54.671
A hundred million.

52:55.463 --> 52:59.092
Was it over once you paid?
Were there any other damages?

52:59.759 --> 53:02.387
My mom runs a café,

53:02.470 --> 53:04.764
but it is in shambles now.

53:05.515 --> 53:06.391
I see.

53:07.934 --> 53:10.645
Is that when you hurt your face?

53:12.105 --> 53:12.981
Yes.

53:15.609 --> 53:16.735
You must feel wronged.

53:18.361 --> 53:19.779
Did you go to the police?

53:20.822 --> 53:21.656
No.

53:24.409 --> 53:26.494
They threatened to kill my mom.

53:27.787 --> 53:28.622
Who?

53:30.248 --> 53:31.458
Their boss.

53:31.541 --> 53:35.086
Delicious hamburgers have arrived.

53:37.631 --> 53:38.757
Hear me out first.

53:45.347 --> 53:46.598
As you heard,

53:46.681 --> 53:48.850
my grandpa is no longer a loan shark.

53:48.934 --> 53:51.353
He provides zero-interest loans
to people in need.

53:51.937 --> 53:53.230
But we occasionally

53:53.313 --> 53:56.316
come across punks who try
to take advantage of his good heart.

53:56.816 --> 53:58.735
Yang Jae-myeong was one of them.

53:59.569 --> 54:02.113
He lied about his mother needing
to get an operation.

54:02.197 --> 54:04.115
He borrowed ten million won and vanished.

54:04.199 --> 54:06.493
It took me half a year to track him down.

54:07.285 --> 54:09.621
I saw him begging
in front of a train station.

54:10.413 --> 54:14.167
At first, I thought Yang Jae-myeong
had really become homeless,

54:14.251 --> 54:18.546
but I noticed how clean his teeth were
as I was passing by.

54:19.506 --> 54:21.007
So I tailed him.

54:21.633 --> 54:25.679
I found out that he and his goons
were pretending to be homeless

54:25.762 --> 54:28.431
and stealing IDs
from actual homeless people.

54:29.182 --> 54:32.769
They use the IDs to create
shell corporations and open bank accounts.

54:32.852 --> 54:34.688
Then they con private loan sharks

54:34.771 --> 54:38.108
and take out loans anywhere
from tens to hundreds of millions of won.

54:39.317 --> 54:41.528
This tactic was so professional,

54:41.611 --> 54:44.406
we thought there would be someone
behind Yang Jae-myeong.

54:45.657 --> 54:49.327
I found out that this person
had ties to Yang Jae-myeong.

54:50.620 --> 54:51.454
Do you know him?

54:56.126 --> 54:57.252
I do.

55:02.632 --> 55:04.718
Our goal today is to get an exact count

55:04.801 --> 55:08.054
of how many IDs
Yang Jae-myeong steals per night.

55:08.138 --> 55:10.265
No matter what happens, stand down.

55:10.348 --> 55:11.850
If they find out we're tailing them,

55:11.933 --> 55:13.560
all my planning
will have been for nothing.

55:17.814 --> 55:19.691
IDENTIFICATION CARD

56:30.929 --> 56:32.889
There are caps in the back.
Cover your face.

56:59.249 --> 57:00.875
Hey. How about this punk?

57:01.376 --> 57:02.627
This bastard is too drunk.

57:02.710 --> 57:04.712
I think he might have something on him.

57:10.760 --> 57:12.303
Sir, there.

57:12.387 --> 57:14.097
Find a bastard who isn't wasted.

57:14.180 --> 57:15.098
Right. Okay.

57:17.058 --> 57:18.309
- Follow me.
- Yes, sir.

57:18.393 --> 57:20.186
- Hey, let's go.
- Okay.

57:41.249 --> 57:42.250
Keep your head down.

57:51.092 --> 57:52.719
Hello, sir.

57:52.802 --> 57:53.720
Yes.

57:54.220 --> 57:58.433
You shouldn't lie down on this cold floor
with just some flimsy newspaper.

57:58.516 --> 58:00.852
You should put something underneath
and lie down.

58:00.935 --> 58:02.020
Right.

58:02.645 --> 58:03.521
Jeez.

58:03.605 --> 58:05.064
When did you last eat?

58:05.148 --> 58:07.400
It must have been a day or two ago.

58:07.484 --> 58:09.694
We aren't shady people.

58:09.777 --> 58:13.156
We're from a homeless association
funded by Seoul.

58:13.239 --> 58:14.449
I see.

58:14.532 --> 58:18.453
The government created this organization
so we could help each other out.

58:18.536 --> 58:20.038
Why don't you join?

58:20.121 --> 58:21.080
Huh?

58:21.164 --> 58:24.250
If you join our organization,
you won't have to sit here like this.

58:24.334 --> 58:26.419
We will find you a job right away.

58:26.503 --> 58:29.756
You will be given 20 masks
free of charge every month.

58:29.839 --> 58:33.885
We will also get the 300,000 won
monthly government stipend for you.

58:33.968 --> 58:34.886
300,000 won…

58:37.180 --> 58:38.014
- Sir.
- Yes.

58:38.097 --> 58:41.559
If you have an ID, we can register you
with the association right away.

58:41.643 --> 58:44.604
Then we can get you
the money by next week.

58:44.687 --> 58:45.730
Do you understand?

58:45.813 --> 58:47.065
- Yes.
- Okay.

58:49.234 --> 58:50.068
Here.

58:51.486 --> 58:53.738
Not anyone can join,
so please keep this a secret.

58:53.821 --> 58:54.697
Okay.

58:55.573 --> 58:56.407
Thank you.

58:56.491 --> 58:58.451
That guy has a silver tongue.

58:58.535 --> 58:59.369
Thank you.

59:02.455 --> 59:03.873
Four IDs so far…

59:15.885 --> 59:17.845
- Excuse me, sir.
- Yes? What is it?

59:18.846 --> 59:21.057
We're from the Homeless Association.

59:21.140 --> 59:24.102
- The thing is--
- You bastard!

59:24.602 --> 59:27.397
Hey, you bastard!
Where is my ID? Give me back my ID!

59:27.480 --> 59:31.192
What? You crazy bastard! Fuck!

59:32.360 --> 59:33.736
Let go, you fucker!

59:37.407 --> 59:39.701
Hey! You can't get involved!

01:01:39.153 --> 01:01:42.115
Subtitle translation by:
